==Serbo-Croatian==
{{wikipedia|lang=sh}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*Bělъgordъ}}. Composed of [[Ekavian]] Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|bȅo||white}} (from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{m|sla-pro|*bělъ}}) and {{m|sh|grȃd||city}} (from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{m|sla-pro|*gordъ}}). The city is named after the white wall of the fortress that enclosed the city. See also {{m|sh|Biograd}}, {{m|ru|Бе́лгород|sc=Cyrl}}, {{m|pl|Białogard}}.

